er><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="Y" name="SEA"  created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-8311615-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>8311615</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="Y" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-9025539-A"  status="new"><document-id status="new"  format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>9025539</doc-number> <kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="Y"  name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-9049016-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country> <doc-number>9049016</doc-number> <kind>A</kind> </document-id><sources><source category="Y" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-9194999-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>9194999</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="Y" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-9324241-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>9324241</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="Y" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1069198A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OKADA YASUTAKA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SUMITOMO METAL IND</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>WATARI KOJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OKADA, YASUTAKA</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SUMITOMO METAL INDUSTRIES, LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>WATARI, KOJI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OKADA YASUTAKA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>WATARI KOJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OKADA, YASUTAKA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>WATARI, KOJI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A machine structural steel product which comprises, in mass %, 0.05 to 0.55 % of C, 0.50 to 2.5 % of Si, 0.01 to 2.00 % of Mn, 0.035 % or less of P, 0.005 to 0.2 % of S and 0.150 % or less of N, and optionally further comprise one or more of Cu, Ni, Cr, Mo, V, Nb, Ti, B, Al, Bi, Ca, Pb, Te, Nd and Se, with the proviso that its chemical composition satisfies the formulae: -23C+Si (5-2Si)-4Mn+104S-3Cr-9V+10 &gt;/= 0 and 3.2C+0.8Mn+5.2S+0.5Cr-120N+2.6Pb+4.1Bi-0.001 alpha &lt;2&gt;+0.13 alpha  &gt;/= 3.0, the balance being Fe and impurities, contains ferrite phase in an amount of 10 to 80 % in the structure thereof, and has a Hv hardness of 160 to 350, wherein  alpha  represents an area ratio of ferrite phase in the structure in terms of %; and structural parts for a machine manufactured from the steel product. The steel product and the structural parts are much excellent in machinability, particularly with respect to "drill life" and "disposability of chips" in drilling. The structural parts can be manufactured with relative ease through machining from the above steel product.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Ce produit en acier, destiné à des pièces structurelles de machines comprend, en pourcentage massique, 0,05 à 0,55 % de C, 0,50 à 2,5 % de Si, 0,01 à 2,00 % de Mn, 0,035 % ou moins de P, 0,005 à 0,2 % de S et 0,150 % ou moins de N, et il comprend éventuellement un ou plusieurs des métaux suivants Cu, Ni, Cr, Mo, V, Nb, Ti, B, Al, Bi, Ca, Pb, Te, Nd et Se, à condition que sa composition chimique corresponde aux formules -23C+Si(5-2Si)-4Mn+104S-3Cr-9V+10 &gt;/= 0, et 3,2C+0,8Mn+5,2S+0,5Cr-120N+2,6Pb+4,1Bi-0,001 alpha &lt;2&gt;+0,13 alpha  &gt;/= 3,0, le solde étant constitué de Fe et d'impuretés; il contient une phase ferrite représentant 10 à 80 % de sa structure et il possède une dureté Hv de l'ordre de 160 à 350; dans ces formules  alpha  représente un rapport de surface de la phase ferrite dans la structure, en terme de pourcentage. L'invention concerne également des pièces structurelles destinées à une machine et fabriquées à partir de ce produit en acier. Ce produit en acier et les pièces structurelles se comportent de manière excellente en ce qui concerne leur capacité d'usinage, notamment en ce qui concerne leur durée de vie de forage et de leur capacité de rejet d'éclats de forage. On peut fabriquer ces pièces structurelles relativement facilement par usinage du produit en acier ci-dessus.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>